.SH NAME
mmt, mvt \- typeset documents, view graphs, and slides
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mmt
[ \fIoptions\fR ] [ \fIfiles\fR ]
.PP
.B mvt
[ \fIoptions\fR ] [ \fIfiles\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
These two commands are very similar to
.BR mm (1).
However, they typeset their input via
.BR troff (1),
rather than formatting it via
.BR nroff (1). 
.sp
\fBMvt\fR is a link to \fBmmt\fR.
.sp
.B Mmt
uses
the
.B MM
macro package,
while
.B mvt
uses the
macro package for
view graphs and slides.
These two commands have options for specifying 
preprocessing by
.BR tbl (1)
and/or
.BR eqn (1).
Depending on the options selected, the proper pipelines and the
required arguments and flags are generated for
.BR troff (1)
and
for
the macro packages.  
.PP
.I Options
are given below.
Any other arguments or flags (e.g.,
.BR \-rC3 )
are passed
to
.BR troff (1)
or to
the macro package,
as appropriate.
Such options can occur in any order,
but they must appear before 
.IR files .
If no arguments are given,
.B mmt
and
.B mvt
print a list of their options.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 10
.B \-a
Invoke the
.B \-a
option of
.BR troff (1).
.sp
.TP
.B \-e
Invoke
.BR eqn (1).
.sp
.TP
.B \-t
Invoke
.BR tbl (1).
.sp
.TP
.B \-y
(For \fBmmt\fR)
Use the non-compacted version of the macros (see
.BR mm (7)).
Ineffective for
.BR mvt .
.PD
.PP
These commands read the standard input when
.B \-
is specified in place of \fIfiles\fR. 
.SH HINT
Use the
.BI \-o list
option of
.BR troff (1)
to specify ranges of pages to be output.
These commands, if invoked with
one or more of the
.BR \-e ,
.BR \-t ,
and
.B \-
options,
together
with the
.BI \-o list
option of
.BR troff (1)
may cause a harmless "broken pipe" diagnostic
if the last page of the document is not specified in
.IR list .
.SH SEE ALSO
.tr ~
.PD 0
env(1), eqn(1), mm(1), tbl(1), troff(1), profile(5),
environ(7), mm(7), mv(7).
.PP
.I "\s-1MM\s+1\-Memorandum Macros\^"
in the ZEUS Utilities Manual.
.PD
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.tr ~~
"m[mv]t: no input file" if none of the arguments is a readable
file and the command is not used as a filter.
